    {
      "id": "claim_87b7649845d342a2a742287bdf02fff4",
      "statement": "Hub teardown runs in two places in handler.Upgrade: the socket close handler (peer.Close() + RemovePeerById, with RemoveHubById when the hub empties) and a fallback right after hub.HandleMessage returns. Both call the idempotent hub.RemovePeerById, which returns false without broadcasting anything when the peer is already gone, so a duplicate removal cannot double-send the PeerDisconnectedMessage or double-trigger RemoveHubById.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/websocket.go#L27-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f156c70d169fa5d2ce1876701e397bc78ec66cee9be78e51704b36a14a4df8fb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/hub/hub.go#L106-L109",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:15265520480f53f84eaf4f5e487468864693bfef626ad8137a4e6bbdd81e7888:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4df69d732b3049588880a9ea4bfaf548",
      "statement": "The server applies a 60 requests/minute ulule/limiter v3 fasthttp middleware keyed by the socket peer address by default, or by the outermost X-Forwarded-For IP only when APP_TRUST_PROXY is set; handler.clientIP applies the same trust logic for IP-keyed hubs so /v1/ip-hubs/* do not collapse behind a reverse proxy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/handler.go",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:b78551509ed1f4345bcc19eea5d03990fc3361d7f7599ff4049b1a1c7332e40a"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_91ae4835b8e64652b68f503c4c27458e",
      "statement": "Zero-downtime migration: an authenticated /v1/admin/migrate?host=<new> call first validates host via validateBackupHost (bare host or host:port, no scheme/path/query/fragment/userinfo, port 0..65535, 400 with no state change on failure); for a valid host it sets backupHost under migrateMu and then atomically flips isMigrating; while migrating, create/join-or-create requests are rejected via ForwardMigrate, which upgrades the connection and sends a going-away close (code 1001) whose reason is the backup host so clients reconnect to the new host.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/migrate.go",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:1083e767529c337e711d65aedf041913410d7bf86ae3d59fcd9bb990822a03e0"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/migrate_test.go",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:1b20c75be3fdd074a05fd88843d204143bbb92ea6790b5a941bec210ff657963"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_379d28f9a4504ca69894f2b9f180016c",
      "statement": "Storage backends are selected by config: MemoryStorage is a mutex-guarded map, and GacheStorage wraps a ntsd/gache/v2 Gache instance with the expired hook disabled and default expiration overridden to NoTTL via SetDefaultExpire (gache's 30s default TTL would otherwise expire live hub/peer entries).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/storage/gache.go",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:a2c095ede439e8bb046806e3bf816c6f529d6e0d69db46f4a86960aec451fbe5"
        },
        {
